#!/usr/sbin/nft -f
#
# Restrict the Ollama API to the trading LXC.
#
# RUNS ON THE OLLAMA LXC (192.168.68.49), not on the trading box. Nothing in
# this repo installs it — see deploy/README-ollama.md.
#
# The companion drop-in (deploy/systemd/ollama.service.d/override.conf) binds
# Ollama to 0.0.0.0 so the backend can reach it at all. Ollama has NO
# AUTHENTICATION of any kind, so on its own that hands every host on the LAN
# an open model API: list models, run generations against the GPU, pull new
# ones, and `DELETE /api/delete` the ones this project depends on. The bind
# and this file are two halves of one change and must be installed together.
#
# Same shape as trading.nft, and for the same reason: bind broadly, then let
# the firewall decide who may connect. Deliberately a SEPARATE table from the
# distro's `inet filter`, so it can be removed wholesale
# (`nft delete table inet ollama_fw`) without touching anything else. In
# nftables every table sees the packet, so a drop here applies regardless of
# what the other table's policy is.
#
# Ordering is load-bearing, exactly as in trading.nft:
#   - `ct state established,related` FIRST, so a mistake in this file cannot
#     cut off the ssh session you are editing it from.
#   - `iif lo accept`, so the LXC can still reach its own API — `ollama run`,
#     `ollama pull` and any local health check all go through 11434.
# Only then the single permitted source, then the drop.
#
# NOT touched: ssh. Locking yourself out of the box that holds the models is
# not a tradeoff worth making for a service that has no auth anyway.
#
# Persist it: this loads the ruleset for the current boot only. Add it to
# /etc/nftables.conf (or /etc/nftables.d/) and `systemctl enable nftables`,
# or it silently disappears on the next restart — and a firewall that is gone
# after a reboot verifies identically to one that works.

table inet ollama_fw {
	chain input {
		type filter hook input priority filter + 10; policy accept;

		ct state established,related accept
		iif lo accept

		# The trading LXC. The ONLY host with any business here.
		ip saddr 192.168.68.107 tcp dport 11434 accept

		tcp dport 11434 drop
	}
}
